   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ifc_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 337,
   "width": 924,
   "height": 195,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100020,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700140,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "SubscriptionRepository -> SqlSubscriptionRepository\n    findActiveForEventType(eventType, tenantId)    # the fan-out match\n    getById(subscriptionId)    # read FRESH at every attempt, never cached\nDeliveryRepository -> SqlDeliveryRepository\n    insertFanOut(eventId, subscriptionId, sequenceNumber)   # idempotent\n    claimNextDue(workerId, limit)     # bounded and SEQUENCE-GATED\n    recordAttempt(deliveryId, outcome, nextAttemptAt | terminal)\nHttpDeliveryClient -> DefaultHttpDeliveryClient\n    send(url, signedPayload, headers, timeout)   # NEVER follows redirects\nSigner -> HmacSha256Signer                 sign(secret, timestamp, payload)\nCircuitBreakerRegistry -> PerSubscriptionCircuitBreaker\n    isOpen / recordSuccess / recordFailure    # PER SUBSCRIPTION, never global\nRetryPolicy -> ExponentialBackoffWithJitter    nextAttemptAt(attemptNumber)",
   "originalText": "SubscriptionRepository -> SqlSubscriptionRepository\n    findActiveForEventType(eventType, tenantId)    # the fan-out match\n    getById(subscriptionId)    # read FRESH at every attempt, never cached\nDeliveryRepository -> SqlDeliveryRepository\n    insertFanOut(eventId, subscriptionId, sequenceNumber)   # idempotent\n    claimNextDue(workerId, limit)     # bounded and SEQUENCE-GATED\n    recordAttempt(deliveryId, outcome, nextAttemptAt | terminal)\nHttpDeliveryClient -> DefaultHttpDeliveryClient\n    send(url, signedPayload, headers, timeout)   # NEVER follows redirects\nSigner -> HmacSha256Signer                 sign(secret, timestamp, payload)\nCircuitBreakerRegistry -> PerSubscriptionCircuitBreaker\n    isOpen / recordSuccess / recordFailure    # PER SUBSCRIPTION, never global\nRetryPolicy -> ExponentialBackoffWithJitter    nextAttemptAt(attemptNumber)",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ifc",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 330,
   "width": 621,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100021,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700147,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "DeliveryWorker is the orchestrator: it depends on all six interfaces and implements\nnone of the storage, network or coordination itself.",
   "originalText": "DeliveryWorker is the orchestrator: it depends on all six interfaces and implements\nnone of the storage, network or coordination itself.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 386,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100022,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700154,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Two details in that list are decisions rather than plumbing. getById is read FRESH\nat every attempt and never cached across retries - a customer who rotates their\nsigning secret or changes their endpoint mid-retry-schedule should have the next\nattempt honour it. And the breaker is keyed PER SUBSCRIPTION: one subscriber's\ndead endpoint must never open a breaker that stops delivery to anyone else.",
   "originalText": "Two details in that list are decisions rather than plumbing. getById is read FRESH\nat every attempt and never cached across retries - a customer who rotates their\nsigning secret or changes their endpoint mid-retry-schedule should have the next\nattempt honour it. And the breaker is keyed PER SUBSCRIPTION: one subscriber's\ndead endpoint must never open a breaker that stops delivery to anyone else.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
