   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100026,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700182,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "UPDATE deliveries SET claimed_by = :worker_id\n WHERE status = 'pending'\n   AND next_attempt_at <= NOW()\n   AND NOT EXISTS (                        -- THE ORDERING GATE\n         SELECT 1 FROM deliveries prior\n          WHERE prior.subscription_id = deliveries.subscription_id\n            AND prior.sequence_number = deliveries.sequence_number - 1\n            AND prior.status = 'pending'   -- prior is not terminal yet\n       )\n ORDER BY next_attempt_at\n LIMIT :limit\nRETURNING *",
   "originalText": "UPDATE deliveries SET claimed_by = :worker_id\n WHERE status = 'pending'\n   AND next_attempt_at <= NOW()\n   AND NOT EXISTS (                        -- THE ORDERING GATE\n         SELECT 1 FROM deliveries prior\n          WHERE prior.subscription_id = deliveries.subscription_id\n            AND prior.sequence_number = deliveries.sequence_number - 1\n            AND prior.status = 'pending'   -- prior is not terminal yet\n       )\n ORDER BY next_attempt_at\n LIMIT :limit\nRETURNING *",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "claim",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 626,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The NOT EXISTS clause is the ENTIRE ordering guarantee, and it is worth being\nprecise about why it has to live inside the claim rather than in front of it: a\nseparate 'is the prior sequence terminal?' read followed by a separate claim is\nexactly the check-then-act race - the prior row could still be MID-COMMIT between\nthe two steps.",
   "originalText": "The NOT EXISTS clause is the ENTIRE ordering guarantee, and it is worth being\nprecise about why it has to live inside the claim rather than in front of it: a\nseparate 'is the prior sequence terminal?' read followed by a separate claim is\nexactly the check-then-act race - the prior row could still be MID-COMMIT between\nthe two steps.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 726,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700196,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Folding the gate into the same WHERE clause the claim itself uses makes 'is N+1\neligible' and 'claim N+1' ONE ATOMIC DECISION.",
   "originalText": "Folding the gate into the same WHERE clause the claim itself uses makes 'is N+1\neligible' and 'claim N+1' ONE ATOMIC DECISION.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 782,
   "width": 576,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And note what counts as terminal: succeeded OR dead_lettered. Giving up on\nsequence N is what unblocks N+1 - so a permanently broken delivery delays the\nqueue by its retry schedule, not forever.",
   "originalText": "And note what counts as terminal: succeeded OR dead_lettered. Giving up on\nsequence N is what unblocks N+1 - so a permanently broken delivery delays the\nqueue by its retry schedule, not forever.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "loopc",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 866,
   "width": 940,
   "height": 290,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100030,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700210,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "loopc_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "loopc_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 853,
   "width": 924,
   "height": 315,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100031,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700217,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "for delivery in due:\n    subscription = subscriptionRepo.getById(delivery.subscription_id)\n\n    if circuitBreaker.isOpen(subscription.id):\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'skipped',\n                      nextAttemptAt=retryPolicy.nextAttemptAt(attempts))\n        continue      # fail fast - NO SOCKET against a known-dead endpoint\n\n    signature = signer.sign(subscription.secret, timestamp, payload)\n    result = httpClient.send(subscription.endpoint_url, payload,\n        headers={'Webhook-Signature': f't={timestamp},v1={signature}',\n                 'Webhook-Id': delivery.id},\n        timeout=SUBSCRIBER_TIMEOUT)\n\n    if result.ok:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'succeeded')        # terminal: unblocks N+1\n    elif delivery.attempt_count >= MAX_ATTEMPTS:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'dead_lettered')   # terminal: unblocks N+1\n    else:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'retry_scheduled',\n                      nextAttemptAt=retryPolicy.nextAttemptAt(attempts))",
   "originalText": "for delivery in due:\n    subscription = subscriptionRepo.getById(delivery.subscription_id)\n\n    if circuitBreaker.isOpen(subscription.id):\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'skipped',\n                      nextAttemptAt=retryPolicy.nextAttemptAt(attempts))\n        continue      # fail fast - NO SOCKET against a known-dead endpoint\n\n    signature = signer.sign(subscription.secret, timestamp, payload)\n    result = httpClient.send(subscription.endpoint_url, payload,\n        headers={'Webhook-Signature': f't={timestamp},v1={signature}',\n                 'Webhook-Id': delivery.id},\n        timeout=SUBSCRIBER_TIMEOUT)\n\n    if result.ok:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'succeeded')        # terminal: unblocks N+1\n    elif delivery.attempt_count >= MAX_ATTEMPTS:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'dead_lettered')   # terminal: unblocks N+1\n    else:\n        recordAttempt(delivery.id, 'retry_scheduled',\n                      nextAttemptAt=retryPolicy.nextAttemptAt(attempts))",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "loopc",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 866,
   "width": 621,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100032,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700224,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "claimNextDue needs no application-level lock, for the same reason the job scheduler\nand payments both push their claims down to the database: many worker instances\nrun concurrently, and a language-level mutex only protects threads on the SAME\ninstance - it does nothing about a different instance claiming the same row a\nmoment later. Correctness comes entirely from the conditional UPDATE's WHERE\nclause, evaluated by the database as one statement.",
   "originalText": "claimNextDue needs no application-level lock, for the same reason the job scheduler\nand payments both push their claims down to the database: many worker instances\nrun concurrently, and a language-level mutex only protects threads on the SAME\ninstance - it does nothing about a different instance claiming the same row a\nmoment later. Correctness comes entirely from the conditional UPDATE's WHERE\nclause, evaluated by the database as one statement.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn5",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": 986,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100033,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700231,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Webhook-Id is what makes at-least-once delivery safe for the subscriber: it is the\nidempotency key they deduplicate on. And Webhook-Signature carries the timestamp\nINSIDE the signed material, so a captured payload cannot be replayed later against\nthe same signature.",
   "originalText": "Webhook-Id is what makes at-least-once delivery safe for the subscriber: it is the\nidempotency key they deduplicate on. And Webhook-Signature carries the timestamp\nINSIDE the signed material, so a captured payload cannot be replayed later against\nthe same signature.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
